Dear founders, operators and technologists,

The Industrial Software Summit returns to Denver on September 15-17, 2026, and the call for proposals is now open.

We are looking for 30-minute talks and 60-minute workshops on:
- AI on the plant floor: deployments, not demos
- Integrating with legacy MES, ERP and historian systems
- Scheduling, quality and maintenance software at mid-market manufacturers
- Buying and selling industrial software: lessons from both sides of the table
- Data infrastructure for operations teams

Proposals are due April 24. Speakers receive a complimentary full-conference pass and travel support for accepted workshops. Customer co-presentations are strongly encouraged.

Submit a proposal: https://indsoftsummit.com/cfp-2026

Last year's summit drew 1,400 attendees from 600 manufacturers and software companies. The 2026 program will be announced in June.

Questions: speakers@indsoftsummit.com

